Specifications (clean-room)
---------------------------

RFC 7230/9110 (HTTP/1.1) + RFC 7541 (HPACK header compression; the
static/Huffman tables and the Appendix C vectors are the RFC's own data) +
RFC 9113 (HTTP/2 framing + stream state machine + flow control; RFC 7540
consulted only where it clarifies the same rules) + RFC 7301 (ALPN — consumed
for h2-over-TLS dispatch, not implemented).

The HTTP/2 DoS mitigations are clean-room from the public CVE-2023-44487 /
CVE-2024-27316 advisories (behavior only).

Conditional requests (ETag/If-* → 304/412) are clean-room from RFC 9110
sec 8.8/13; the HTTP-date parser follows RFC 9110 sec 5.6.7 (all three
formats) with the days-from-civil epoch conversion (Howard Hinnant's public
algorithm).

Request-body parsing is clean-room from RFC 9110 sec 5.6.6 (Content-Type media
type + parameters), the WHATWG URL `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` rules,
and RFC 7578 / RFC 2046 sec 5.1 (multipart/form-data).

The Range request-header parser is clean-room from RFC 7233 sec 2.1
(byte-range-set); the 206 resolution + Content-Range emitter follows RFC 7233
sec 4.

The content-negotiation parsers are clean-room from RFC 9110 sec 12.5.1
(Accept media-range) + sec 12.4.2 (qvalue) + sec 12.5.3 (Accept-Encoding) and
RFC 4647 sec 3.3.1 (Accept-Language basic filtering).

Clean-room from the RFCs, no HPACK/HTTP-2/nghttp2 source consulted or copied;
TLS via Zig `std.crypto.tls`.

The reverse-proxy handler (`http.proxy`) is clean-room from RFC 9110 sec 7.6
(hop-by-hop fields, Via) + the RFC 7239 / de-facto `X-Forwarded-*` headers; the
`SO_REUSEPORT` thread-per-core accept engine is a standard kernel-load-balancing
technique (no source consulted).

`http.sse` is clean-room from the WHATWG HTML "server-sent events" standard
(the `text/event-stream` wire format: event/id/retry/data fields, multi-line
data, comment lines). No third-party source consulted or copied.

Design references (behavior only, no source copied)
---------------------------------------------------

  - lalinsky/dusty (**MIT**) — the 1.1 client shape.
  - Go `net/http` (**BSD-3-Clause**, The Go Authors) — redirect semantics,
    server shape, gzip handler.
  - Go `net/http/httputil.ReverseProxy` (**BSD-3-Clause**) and nginx
    `proxy_pass` (**BSD-2-Clause**) — the reverse-proxy behavior.
